A||N||10||Bob Englert||NC Fiero owners meeting Saturday in Raleigh||||14||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||01-31-2001||06:50 PM||||We have found a location for the Feb 3rd Fiero meeting in Raleigh!  We will<BR>be meeting at Ryan's Steakhouse at 2:00PM at 200 Crossroad Blvd. in Cary.<BR>This is right off I-40 and US-1 and is very easy to get to.  It is in the<BR>middle of Crossroads Shopping Center so there will be plenty of parking.<P>From I-40 take exit 293 to US-1 South.  Take the first exit right but then<BR>be prepared to go left over US-1 before the traffic light and you will be in<BR>the shopping center.  Ryan's will be on your right.  You will not actually<BR>get on US-1 from I-40.  The shopping center is only a couple of blocks off<BR>of I-40.<P>If anyone will be driving through Greensboro to the meeting let me know if<BR>you would like to meet and drive over in a group.  We could meet at the I-40<BR>rest area near Burlington and convoy over.  I always like to see a pack of<BR>Fieros on the highway!<P>I look forward to seeing many of you from our first meeting and many new<BR>Fiero owners.  Bring your Fiero if you can, but I look forward to meeting<BR>all with an interest in our favorite 2 seater!<P>I just learned that Ed and Rosy Parks will be delivering and picking up a<BR>customer's Fiero in NC and should be able to attend our meeting and lunch.<BR>I look forward to seeing them and having them join us on Saturday.<P>Call or email if you have any questions.  (336) 854-5865<P>Bob Englert<BR>Greensboro, NC<P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||bHooper||01-31-2001||09:01 PM||||Yep, meeting in Raliegh should be lots of fun!<P>but not as fun as driving down the highway without any exhaust manifolds!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/puke_1.gif">    <BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroWife||01-31-2001||09:25 PM||||We live in Ohio but my Grandparents live in Fayetteville.  I'd love to go out to see them sometime in May.  I might be able to drag 87ECO5 (Scott) out there if we could meet up with some of the Carolina Fieros along the way.  Please let me know if there is anything shaking in May.  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/fierowife/Signature.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Bob Englert||01-31-2001||09:29 PM||||There are some great Fiero roads in the western part of the state that should be on the way from OH.  We plan to try to organize some weekend fun runs in the mountains when the weather warms up in the spring and summer.<P>Will keep the group informed, the more the better!<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||01-31-2001||09:54 PM||||Yeah don't forget us down here in SC  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||MEC91Firebird||01-31-2001||11:17 PM||||Is there a web site for the group?  Im from Westren NC, and would be intrested in knowing more, Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||01-31-2001||11:23 PM||||We don't have a web site.  We have just started meeting, had our first one in Dec in Greensboro.  We are trying to see how much interest there is to begin to develop an informal group of Fiero owners.  <P>I would like to meet in different parts of the state to involve as many owners as possible.  Obviously we will tend to meet where there is the most interest.  My favorite fiero activity is to explore the twisty mountain back roads, and I would like to arrange several informal runs when the weather improves.<P>Right now we are trying to see if there is interest in forming a 'real' club or if we should just keep it loose and informal.<P>If you can, come on over and have lunch and meet some other owners.  We have one coming from Hickory right now I think.<P>I will add you to my email list so you will get future announcements.  Hope to meet you soon!<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||02-01-2001||09:09 AM||||I'll be there!  Just bought my first Fiero last Monday.  Just in time for the first Raleigh gathering.  Hoping to get some other friends of mine with Fieros to come, too.  The bartender may be working, but LZeitgeist will be there (he's responsible for getting me hooked on our Plastic Fantastic many years ago...)<P>See you Saturday!<P>------------------<BR>When you choke a smurf, what color does it turn?||||reg||6
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||02-01-2001||01:52 PM||||Yup, I'm coming in my red Formula, and my Dad will be coming with his (formerly my) '88 4-cyl. Coupe (used to be red, but is now white, awaiting the full Pace Car Replica treatment...)<P>Gotta polish mine up before I get there, though... can't let Smurf-Choker's Formula look better than mine...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
